# Project Notes

> **For future Claude**: This directory contains active and archived project notes. All notes follow the `type: project` schema.

## Frontmatter Schema
```yaml
---
date: YYYY-MM-DD              # creation
updated: YYYY-MM-DD           # last meaningful update
type: project
tags: [project, ...]
status: active                # active | planning | completed | archived | on-hold
related-people: ["[[People/...]]", ...]
related-projects: ["[[Projects/...]]", ...]
job: Work                     # optional - which job/board context
repo: /path/or/git-url        # optional - enables git + docs checks
graduated-from: "[[Idea]]"    # optional - set by /obsidian-graduate
ai-first: true
---
```

## Note Structure
Each project note should contain:
- `## For future Claude` preamble
- `## Overview` - What the project is and why it exists
- `## Recent Activity` - Last 30 days of work
- `## Key Decisions` - Major directional choices with rationale
- `## Open Questions` - Unresolved issues
- `## Related` - Links to other projects, people, concepts

## Naming Convention
- Use proper names: `gamebus-presenced.md`
- Use kebab-case for multi-word names
